# NeoJaundice

## Neonatal Jaundice Screening and Bilirubin Level Estimation Using Smartphone Skin Images

NeoJaundice is a research-oriented computer vision and machine
learning project investigating neonatal jaundice screening and
bilirubin level estimation from smartphone skin images.

The project aims to develop a modular AI system with reproducible
machine learning experiments, explainability, backend APIs,
a frontend application, and MLOps infrastructure.

## Project Status

Current Phase: Phase 1 - Project Setup

Status: Under Development

No clinically validated prediction model is currently available.

## Intended Capabilities

- Smartphone image validation
- Facial region-of-interest extraction
- Skin segmentation
- Image preprocessing
- Color feature extraction
- Jaundice screening research
- Bilirubin regression research
- EfficientNet-based deep learning
- GradCAM explainability
- FastAPI inference API
- React frontend
- PostgreSQL integration
- Docker deployment
- MLflow experiment tracking
- DVC dataset versioning
- Automated testing and CI/CD
- Model monitoring
- ONNX model export

